# Day 40/50 — Distributed Systems

What happens when multiple computers work together but exist in different locations?

They can form a **Distributed System**

A distributed system consists of multiple independent computers that communicate and coordinate to achieve a common goal.
From online banking to cloud platforms and large-scale applications, distributed systems help services operate across multiple machines.

But coordination isn't always easy.

Machines can fail, networks can become unavailable, and information may take time to synchronize.
Yet the system is designed to keep working despite these challenges.

And perhaps that's the most interesting part.

Working together doesn't mean everything will always go perfectly. It means having ways to handle things when they don't.

**Because true strength isn't about never facing failure. It's about continuing to function even when one part of the system does.**
